    {
      "blockId": "tour:lead:e3456bc1f4d270f4",
      "field": "lead",
      "sourceTextSha256": "968353891e9b4cdb0959816026564a01cd3d57feabb7bf813aa486516195224f",
      "text": "The journey begins in La Paz, the world’s highest seat of government, then takes you to the famous mirror-like Uyuni Salt Flats. It crosses the high Altiplano to the Atacama, the driest non-polar desert on Earth, before flying to Santiago. It then turns south to Chilean Patagonia: Torres del Paine and its granite towers, then the Marble Caves of Lake General Carrera and the San Rafael Glacier, calving icebergs into turquoise waters. It ends in Santiago, with Viña Vik and a day on the Pacific coast in Valparaíso.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1iDDWJn3nE4yuEwxneW1nVevFt5fD4-Vw",
